#
# SilkXotic v1.1 "Charmeuse" — zram compressor: lz4 -> zstd (roadmap 🥇).
# Layered after silkxotic-opts.config. Pairs with the one-line source default in
# drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c (default_compressor "lz4" -> "zstd").
#
# CRYPTO_ZSTD only makes zstd AVAILABLE to zram (it self-selects ZSTD_COMPRESS/
# ZSTD_DECOMPRESS + acomp). CRYPTO_LZ4 stays =y, so BOTH algorithms are built in and
# you can A/B them at runtime via /sys/block/zram0/comp_algorithm (root, before disksize
# is set) without rebuilding. ZRAM_WRITEBACK stays on.
#
# CAVEAT (must verify on-device): the kernel source default only wins if crDroid's
# userspace does NOT write comp_algorithm at boot. The active algo is the bracketed one
# in `cat /sys/block/zram0/comp_algorithm`. The vendor already patched the kernel default
# to "lz4" (upstream 4.14 is "lzo"), which suggests the kernel default IS honored here.
CONFIG_CRYPTO_ZSTD=y
